# Auto prod rebuild

Daily UI work prefers **`pnpm prod`** (faster serve) over `pnpm dev`.

## Automation (already installed)

1. `afterFileEdit` marks `apps/web` / `apps/api` (and shared packages) dirty in `.cursor/hooks-state/pending-build.json`
2. On agent **stop**, dirty packages are built (`pnpm --filter … build`)
3. If `:4002` / `:4001` were listening, those processes are restarted so `pnpm prod` picks up the new build

Opt out for a session: `NESY_AUTO_PROD_BUILD=0`

Log: `.cursor/hooks-state/auto-prod-build.log`

## Agent habit (belt-and-suspenders)

When you finish web/api source changes and the user is on prod, you may still run:

```bash
pnpm --filter @nesy/web build
```

Do not start `pnpm dev` just to preview agent edits unless the user asks.
